#
# prima-materia — Christian theosophy, taken off the register
#
# Taken from traditions/registry-western-esoteric.ttl on the structure-driven
# entrance of SPEC 14. The first work opened is not one of the two named in the
# registration but the dialogue Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of
# Der Weg zu Christo, because it is the shortest work of the corpus that
# prescribes practices and states what follows from neglecting them, which is
# what the testability-driven entrance of the same section asks for first.
# Aurora and De signatura rerum stand below as unopened works.
#
# Read at the wording on 2026-11-20 by one reader over the whole booklet, in
# the German of the reprint of 1732; the harvest is not the two-pass harvest of
# prima-materia#893 and claims no completeness beyond the passages read.
# Identifiers are formed from the German of the edition. Conditions of failure
# carry a note beginning "Counted as a condition of failure", signs of success
# one beginning "Counted as a sign of success".
#

pmt:ChristianTheosophy a pm:Tradition ;
    rdfs:label "Christian theosophy"@en, "Christliche Theosophie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Böhme's transmission of a divine self-disclosure through opposition, reported as having been seen rather than reasoned."@en ;
    skos:note "Read at the wording on 2026-11-20: Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, in the reprint of 1732, cited by page from the running heads and by the numbered answers of the dialogue; one reader over the whole booklet, 111 records, 111 nodes in this file."@en ;
    skos:note "The contact route stays at documented, as the registration set it; the booklet names no source but scripture and does not test the route. Agreement with the later reception (the English translations in the line of Sparrow and Law) is reception."@en ;
    pm:principalCorpus "Böhme, Aurora; Böhme, De signatura rerum; Böhme, Der Weg zu Christo" ;
    pm:corpusWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben, pmw:DerWegZuChristo, pmw:Aurora, pmw:DeSignaturaRerum ;
    pm:coverageState pm:placesEntered ;
    pm:contactRoute pm:contactRouteDocumented ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 165, §1-3; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben .

pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:label "Vom übersinnlichen Leben"@en, "Vom übersinnlichen Leben"@de ;
    skos:note "Böhme. A dialogue between a master and a disciple, first printed in Der Weg zu Christo (Görlitz, 1624), the only collection of his writings printed in his lifetime; the dating and the attribution are not disputed in the literature consulted for the landscape. The copy read is the reprint in Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein, printed after the Amsterdam copy in 1732, by the title leaf of the collection and of the booklet in the text layer. Opened and read complete on 2026-11-20."@en ;
    skos:note "Read on 2026-11-20 in the full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm (Getty Research Institute copy), long s normalised; pp. 165-188, the running heads of pp. 166 and 186 lost and placed by sequence, those of pp. 171, 178 and 185 misprinted or misread and corrected by sequence. The layer loses one page: the end of answer 5, answers 6 and 7 and the start of answer 8, which the English carries as the three things requisite (to resign the will to God, to hate one's own will, to submit under the cross). They are not entered, because nodes rest on the German. The two other German layers in the same archive (derwegzuchristo00bhgoog and bub_gb_7zE3AAAAMAAJ, both of 1715) are Fraktur OCR without a readable word and do not close the gap; a better scan of that page is owed."@en ;
    skos:note "Translations. The English read for comparison is The Way to Christ (Canterbury: G. Moreton, 1894, archive item in.ernet.dli.2015.69053), which calls the dialogue the fourth book and dates it 1624; it stands in the line of John Sparrow's translation. It renders one hour as for a while in answer 2, adds section headings, puts an epigraph from 1 Corinthians 2 in place of the explanation of the title figure, and adds a phrase to the first member of the five-part account of love in answer 27. The editions of 1752 and 1775 in the same archive stand in the same line, so only one translator was read; Erb's translation of 1978 is lending-restricted. The English was compared with the German for answers 1-9, 14-15, 27, 34-37, 45, 49 and 52-56 only."@en ;
    skos:note "Harvest counts: nine signs of success announced in advance, four tied in the text to the hour of breaking the will off from the creatures and the rest to the way as a whole (radiance of God's glory over the will, the unspeakable love tasted within, the cross turned to a benefit, the body drawn into the following of Christ, rejoicing in the world's hatred, loving what now seems hard, worldly wisdom seen as folly, the love felt burning in soul and body, the wish to die rather than return to the Something). Ten conditions of failure, every one placing the failure on the will of the person: own willing, hearing and seeing; the creatures living in the will; grasping at love; seeking it in a Something; refusing resignation; waiting for an imputed satisfaction. None sets a deadline, and none names an outcome another person could observe; the one span stated is the hour of answers 2 and 15, which is the length of the practice and not a time after which it counts as failed. The work warns in advance that even the holy soul cannot fully feel the light in this life (answer 39), which makes the absence of the announced signs no evidence against the practice."@en .

pmw:DerWegZuChristo a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:label "Der Weg zu Christo"@en, "Der Weg zu Christo"@de ;
    skos:note "Böhme. The collection of nine booklets in the reprint of 1732 (Von wahrer Busse, Vom heiligen Gebet, Ein Schlüssel göttlicher Geheimnüsse, Von wahrer Gelassenheit, Von der Wiedergeburth, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, Von göttlicher Beschaulichkeit, Von der erleuchteten und unerleuchteten Seele, Von den vier Complexionen); the sixth is entered as its own work, pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben. The other eight are unopened; the same text layer (derwegzuchristov00bohm) carries them and is readable, with running heads by booklet."@en .

pmw:Aurora a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:label "Aurora, oder Morgenröte im Aufgang"@en, "Aurora, oder Morgenröte im Aufgang"@de ;
    skos:note "Böhme, written 1612, named in the registration. Unopened; no edition chosen."@en .

pmw:DeSignaturaRerum a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:label "De signatura rerum"@en, "De signatura rerum"@de ;
    skos:note "Böhme, 1622, named in the registration. Unopened; no edition chosen."@en .


pmc:ChristianTheosophyTitelprogrammGoettlichesSchauenHoerenKindschaft a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Title programme: divine vision and hearing, childship, passage into God"@en, "Titelprogramm: göttliches Schauen und Hören, Kindschaft, Übergang in Gott"@de ;
    skos:definition "Programme of the booklet per its title: how the soul attains divine vision and hearing, what its childship in natural and supernatural life is, how it passes from nature into God and back into the nature of selfhood, and what its salvation and ruin are."@en ;
    skos:note "Title page; subject word of the soul garbled in OCR (\"Wie en möge\"). Title page also: \"Gestellet durch Jacob Boehme\", reprint 1732."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: Göttliche Anschauung und Gehör; Selbheit."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), the explanation of the title figure, unpaginated; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyEinaeugigesSchauenEinheitGottes a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Single-eyed vision of God's unity"@en, "Einäugiges Schauen der Einheit Gottes"@de ;
    skos:definition "The soul, made in and after God's image so that it should know, behold and love him alone, regains this vision instead of looking at the manifoldness of creatures."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: Beschaulichkeit und Erkänntnuß."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), the explanation of the title figure, unpaginated; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmp:ChristianTheosophyWillenWirbelpunktKreaturliebeErheben a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Lifting the will out of the whirl-point of creature-love"@en, "Den Willen aus dem Wirbelpunkt der Kreaturliebe erheben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: (1) withdraw the will from attachment to the many creatures; (2) let it rest in Christ's death; (3) renounce the second, outward-looking eye that beholds natural multiplicity."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: Würbel-Punct."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), the explanation of the title figure, unpaginated; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyWillenserhebungFuehrtEinaeugigenGottesschauen a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Raising the will yields single-eyed vision of God"@en, "Willenserhebung führt zum einäugigen Gottesschauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Lifting the will out of creature-love and resting in Christ's death yields the single-eyed vision of God's unity."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChristianTheosophyWillenWirbelpunktKreaturliebeErheben ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChristianTheosophyEinaeugigesSchauenEinheitGottes ;
