pmc:ChristianTheosophyVielerleiLiebeFuehrtZerruettungUnruhe a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Many loves bring disorder, unrest and anguish"@en, "Vielerlei Liebe führt zu Zerrüttung, Unruhe und Angst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Many creatures awaken many lusts; whoever loves much is in turn loved, lured, impregnated, driven and turned about by many; the end is disorder, unrest, constant anguish and aversion, shaped by the reason-heaven in bestial transient lusts that death consumes."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: Vernunfft-Himmel."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChristianTheosophyWillenWirbelpunktKreaturliebeErheben ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), the explanation of the title figure, unpaginated; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyZweiaeugigesSchauenVielheitVerhindertGottesschau a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Two-eyed gazing at multiplicity bars the vision of God"@en, "Zweiäugiges Schauen der Vielheit verhindert die Gottesschau"@de ;
    skos:definition "Looking with two eyes at the discord and manifoldness of nature and creatures scatters the will, inflames and captures it in lust-desire, and makes the spirit put on a bestial misshape in which it can never see God nor inherit blessedness."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure; it concerns pmc:ChristianTheosophyEinaeugigesSchauenEinheitGottes."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: Thierische Mißgestalt."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), the explanation of the title figure, unpaginated; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophySternenNaturkraefteWertlosOhneGottebenbildliche a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Astral and natural powers worthless without the God-image"@en, "Sternen- und Naturkräfte wertlos ohne die gottebenbildliche Gestalt"@de ;
    skos:definition "All the power of the stars and all the might of animals in senses, thought, cleverness, force and pleasure would be useless if we lost our own form, made from and after God so that we know, behold and love him alone."@en ;
    skos:note "Rejects the value of astral and natural powers apart from the God-image; relevant to the capacity hierarchy."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: eigene Gestalt."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), the explanation of the title figure, unpaginated; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyUebersinnlichesLebenGottSehenReden a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Supersensual life: seeing God and hearing him speak; hearing unspeakable words of God within."@en, "Übersinnliches Leben: Gott sehen und reden hören; unaussprechliche Worte Gottes in sich hören."@de ;
    skos:definition "The goal the disciple asks for; the Master places it within the person (§2: it is in you)."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: übersinnliches Leben."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
