pmc:ChristianTheosophyEwigesHoerenSehenSprechenOffenbart a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Eternal hearing, seeing and speaking revealed within; God hears and sees through the person."@en, "Ewiges Hören, Sehen, Sprechen offenbart sich innen; Gott hört und sieht durch einen."@de ;
    skos:definition "§4: in silence one coincides with what God was prior to nature and creatures, perceiving by the very organ through which God perceived in one before self-will arose."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 165, §3; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyStillstehenSelbheitFuehrtEwigemHoeren a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Stilling selfhood yields eternal hearing and seeing"@en, "Stillstehen der Selbheit führt zu ewigem Hören und Sehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Standing still from selfhood's thinking and willing yields the revealed eternal hearing and seeing in which God perceives through the person."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChristianTheosophyStillstehenSinnenWollenSelbheit ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChristianTheosophyEwigesHoerenSehenSprechenOffenbart ;
