pmc:ChristianTheosophySchweigenEinsseinGottVorSchoepfung a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Silence as identity with God before creation"@en, "Schweigen als Einssein mit Gott vor der Schöpfung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Model of divine perception: in silence the person coincides with God as he was prior to nature and creatures (the stuff of which his nature was made); he then perceives by the organ through which God perceived in him before self-will arose."@en ;
    skos:note "Explains why silence of the will, not effort, is the means."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 165, §4; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyEigenwilleStrebenGegenUrsprungHalten a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-will and striving against one's origin hold one back"@en, "Eigenwille und Streben gegen den Ursprung halten zurück"@de ;
    skos:definition "What holds one back: self-willing, self-hearing and self-seeing, plus striving against that from which one came; with one's own willing one breaks oneself off (from God's willing)."@en ;
    skos:note "Answer breaks off mid-sentence at the foot of p. 165; the rest of §5, all of §6-7 and the start of §8 are missing in this OCR text."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure; it concerns pmc:ChristianTheosophyUebersinnlichesLebenGottSehenReden."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 165, §5; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyAeussereHerrschaftKreaturenErzeugtTierische a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Outward rule over creatures breeds bestial nature"@en, "Äußere Herrschaft über Kreaturen erzeugt tierische Art"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ruling over creatures only outwardly is a dominion in bestial manner, an image-bound transient rule; one leads one's desire into bestial essence, becomes infected and captured by it and acquires a bestial nature."@en ;
    skos:note "Fragment; the start of the sentence (and the disciple's question) is lost; inferred subject from context of the surviving clause only. Running head of p. 166 lost in OCR; page placed by sequence."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: bildliche Herrschung."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChristianTheosophyBildlicheArtVerlassen ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 166, §8; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyUeberbildlichkeitHerrschaftGrundNichtsVerletzbar a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Beyond-image state: rule in the ground, unharmed by anything"@en, "Überbildlichkeit: Herrschaft im Grund, von nichts verletzbar"@de ;
    skos:definition "Standing in the beyond-image state: ruling in the ground over all creatures from which they were made; nothing on earth can harm one, since one is equal to all things and nothing is unequal to one."@en ;
    skos:note "Continues onto p. 167 (\"Erden nichts schaden\"). Running head of p. 166 lost in OCR; page placed by sequence."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: Uberbildlichkeit."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 166, §8; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmp:ChristianTheosophyBildlicheArtVerlassen a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Leaving the image-bound mode"@en, "Die bildliche Art verlassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Leave the image-bound mode (bildliche Art) of ruling and desiring."@en ;
    skos:note "Only the condition survives in the fragment. Running head of p. 166 lost in OCR; page placed by sequence."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: bildliche Art."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 166, §8; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyVerlassenBildlichenArtFuehrtUeberbildlichkeit a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Leaving image-bound mode yields the beyond-image state"@en, "Verlassen der bildlichen Art führt in die Überbildlichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Leaving the image-bound mode yields standing in the beyond-image state and ruling in the ground."@en ;
    skos:note "Running head of p. 166 lost in OCR; page placed by sequence."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChristianTheosophyBildlicheArtVerlassen ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChristianTheosophyUeberbildlichkeitHerrschaftGrundNichtsVerletzbar ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 166, §8; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyDingenGleich a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Being equal to all things"@en, "Allen Dingen gleich sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being equal to all things: free of all things and at once ruling over all; a nothing to all things and they a nothing to one; understanding things like a child, without their touching one's sensibility, in the way God rules and sees all things yet nothing grasps him."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: allen Dingen gleich; ohne Berührung deiner Empfindlichkeit."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 167, §9; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmp:ChristianTheosophyKindAllemBesitzEntsagen a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Becoming as a child: forsaking all possession"@en, "Werden wie ein Kind: allem Besitz entsagen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: (1) forsake all things; (2) withdraw desire from them; (3) take nothing into desire as own possession (\"Etwas\"); (4) remain as a child that does not understand what a thing is."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: Eigenthum; Annehmlichkeit."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 167, §9; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyNichtsBegehrenFuehrtGleichheitDingen a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Desiring nothing yields equality with all things"@en, "Nichts begehren führt zur Gleichheit mit allen Dingen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Taking nothing into one's desire yields freedom from all things and rule over all, i.e. being equal to all things."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChristianTheosophyKindAllemBesitzEntsagen ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChristianTheosophyDingenGleich ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 167, §9; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyBesitzBindetBesitzerVerteidigung a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Possession binds the possessor to defend it"@en, "Besitz bindet den Besitzer an seine Verteidigung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Mechanism of possession: as soon as one takes a Something into desire as property, it becomes one thing with oneself and works in one will with one; one is then obliged to protect and care for it as one's own being."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: das Etwas."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 167, §9; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyRuheOhneBeruehrungKreaturenWille a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Rest untouched by creatures, will walking in heaven"@en, "Ruhe ohne Berührung durch Kreaturen, Wille im Himmel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rest such that no creature touches one: with the body in the world among the properties, with reason under the cross of Christ, but with the will walking in heaven at the end from which all creatures came; seeing all things outwardly with reason and inwardly with the mind, and ruling with Christ in and over all things."@en ;
    skos:note "Continues onto p. 168."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: Ruhe; Gemüthe."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 167, §9; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmp:ChristianTheosophyWilleBegierdeGanzChristusUebergeben a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Wholly yielding will and desire to Christ"@en, "Wille und Begierde ganz an Christus übergeben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wholly yield oneself into the life of Jesus Christ, hand over one's willing and desire to him entirely, and will nothing without him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 167, §9; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyEigenesVermoegenErreichtRuheErgebung a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Own ability cannot reach the rest; yielding to Christ required"@en, "Eigenes Vermögen erreicht die Ruhe nicht; Ergebung an Christus nötig"@de ;
    skos:definition "The rest untouched by creatures cannot be reached by one's own ability; only by wholly yielding into the life of Christ."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChristianTheosophyWilleBegierdeGanzChristusUebergeben ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChristianTheosophyRuheOhneBeruehrungKreaturenWille ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without it one can in one's own power not come to the rest at all (\"nichts\")." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 167, §9; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyErgebungChristusFuehrtHimmlischenRuhe a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Yielding to Christ yields the heavenly rest"@en, "Ergebung an Christus führt zur himmlischen Ruhe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wholly yielding will and desire to Christ yields the rest in which the will walks in heaven and rules with Christ over all things."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChristianTheosophyWilleBegierdeGanzChristusUebergeben ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChristianTheosophyRuheOhneBeruehrungKreaturenWille ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 167, §9; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyInnewohnendeKreaturenVerhindernVoelligeErgebung a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Indwelling creatures prevent full surrender"@en, "Innewohnende Kreaturen verhindern die völlige Ergebung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Obstacle named by the disciple: the creatures that live in him hold him back so that he cannot wholly yield, however much he wishes."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure; it concerns pmp:ChristianTheosophyWilleBegierdeGanzChristusUebergeben."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 168, §10; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyGeistWohntWillenKreaturenLeib a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Spirit dwells in the will, creatures in the body"@en, "Geist wohnt im Willen, Kreaturen im Leib"@de ;
    skos:definition "Will-body model: when the will goes out from the creatures they are left, die in the will and live only in the body in the world; if the will does not lead itself into them, the soul stays untouched by them. The Holy Spirit dwells in the will, the creatures in the body."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 168, §10; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmp:ChristianTheosophyWillenChristiWortenBleiben a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Abiding with the will in Christ's words"@en, "Mit dem Willen in Christi Worten bleiben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Remain with one's will in the words of Christ; then his word and spirit remain in one."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 168, §11; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyInnewohnendenHeiligenGeistBewahren a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Retaining the indwelling Holy Spirit"@en, "Den innewohnenden Heiligen Geist bewahren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keeping the indwelling Holy Spirit in the mind's will so that it does not depart."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 168, §11; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyBleibenChristiWortenBewahrtGeist a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Abiding in Christ's words keeps his Spirit"@en, "Bleiben in Christi Worten bewahrt seinen Geist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Remaining with the will in Christ's words keeps his word and spirit within."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChristianTheosophyWillenChristiWortenBleiben ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChristianTheosophyInnewohnendenHeiligenGeistBewahren ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
