pmp:ChristianTheosophyVerlassenWasLiebtLiebenWas a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Leaving what loves one, loving what hates one"@en, "Verlassen, was liebt; lieben, was hasst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: (1) identify what loves one through the will's care (bodily creatures, admirers); (2) let the will leave them and regard them as enemies; (3) accept the world's scorn as Christ's cross; (4) use it daily as exercise of repentance."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: tägliche Übung deiner Busse."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 168, §12-13; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyLiebenWasHasstErhaeltTaegliche a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Loving what hates one sustains the daily dying"@en, "Lieben, was hasst, erhält das tägliche Sterben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Leaving what loves one and loving what hates one sustains the perpetual repentance and with it the daily dying of the creatures."@en ;
    skos:note "Text: by this one can stand in such continual repentance always; capacity linked is the state §11 says repentance produces."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChristianTheosophyVerlassenWasLiebtLiebenWas ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChristianTheosophyTaeglichesSterbenKreaturenTaeglicheHimmelfahrt ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 168, §12; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyUebungHaeltSucheNachEwiger a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Exercise keeps one seeking eternal rest"@en, "Die Übung hält auf der Suche nach ewiger Ruhe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Effect of the exercise: one constantly has reason to hate oneself along with the creature and to look for that everlasting rest where the will can repose."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 169, §13; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmp:ChristianTheosophyStuendlichesEinschwingenGottesBarmherzigkeitChristi a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Hourly swinging into God's mercy and Christ's passion"@en, "Stündliches Einschwingen in Gottes Barmherzigkeit und Christi Leiden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: (1) hourly; (2) leave all creatures in mind; (3) pass above sensual reason; (4) throw oneself into God's mercy and Christ's passion; (5) yield into it."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: einschwingen."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 169, §14; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyKraftSuendeTodTeufelHoelle a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Power over sin, death, devil, hell and world"@en, "Kraft über Sünde, Tod, Teufel, Hölle und Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Power to master sin, death, devil, hell and the world, and to stand firm in every temptation (Anfechtung)."@en ;
