pmc:ChristianTheosophyGuteFreundeGliederChristusGewinnen a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Gaining good friends as members in Christ"@en, "Gute Freunde als Glieder in Christus gewinnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Social consequence: the person gains the hearts of all good friends as his own and loses only enemies who loved his vanity; all souls belonging to Christ become brothers and members of his own life, as branches of one tree; many unknown friends (like Nicodemus) love him in secret."@en ;
    skos:note "Running head misprinted/misread as 271."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 171, §20-21; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyZeichenSpaeterLiebenWasJetzt a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sign: later loving the contempt now feared"@en, "Zeichen: später lieben, was jetzt schwer scheint"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign: what now seems hard (being despised by all the world) one will later love most."@en ;
    skos:note "Running head misprinted/misread as 271."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success, announced in advance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 171, §22; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyZeichenHimmlischeWeisheitEntlarvtWeltweisheit a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sign: heavenly wisdom reveals worldly wisdom as folly"@en, "Zeichen: himmlische Weisheit entlarvt Weltweisheit als Torheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign: once clothed with heavenly wisdom one sees all worldly wisdom is folly, that the world hates only one's enemy, the mortal life, and one begins to love contempt of the mortal body."@en ;
    skos:note "Begins p. 171, continues p. 172. Running head misprinted/misread as 271."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success, announced in advance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 171, §23; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyGoettlichenGrundLiebenIchheitHassen a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Loving the divine ground, hating I-ness"@en, "Den göttlichen Grund lieben, die Ichheit hassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Self-love and self-hatred reconciled: one loves oneself not as one's own (Deinheit) but as a given love of God, the divine ground in oneself; one hates oneself as the Deinheit to which evil clings, wishing to break the I-ness entirely so that it becomes a wholly divine ground. Love hates I-ness because I-ness is a mortal thing; love possesses heaven, I-ness the world."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: Deinheit; Ichheit."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 172, §24; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyLiebeBrauchtLeidGegenstand a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Love needs suffering to have an object"@en, "Liebe braucht Leid als Gegenstand"@de ;
    skos:definition "Why love and suffering must coexist: if love did not stand in suffering it would have nothing to love; because its object, the poor soul, stands in pain, it has cause to love and rescue it; without this love could not be known."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 172, §25; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyFuenfgliedrigesSchemaLiebeNichts a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Five-part schema of love: Nothing and All"@en, "Fünfgliedriges Schema der Liebe: Nichts und Alles"@de ;
    skos:definition "Five-part schema of love: its virtue is the Nothing; its power pervades all things; its height equals God's; its greatness greater than God; whoever finds it finds Nothing and All. Each member is then explained in §27."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: das Nichts; Nichts und Alles."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Jacob Böhme, in Vom übersinnlichen Leben" ;
    dcterms:date "1624"^^xsd:gYear ;
