pmc:ChristianTheosophyKoenigtumGottesWerkeGefundeneLiebe a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Kingship over God's works through finding love"@en, "Königtum über Gottes Werke durch gefundene Liebe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Finding love: being led by it as high as God himself (as Christ's humanity was led to the highest throne); coming into the ground from which all things came and being therein king of all God's works; love leads out of anguish into God and reveals the hidden God within."@en ;
    skos:note "Explanation spans pp. 173-174."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: Ungrund."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 174, §27; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyLiebeUngrund a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Love as groundless abyss (Ungrund)"@en, "Liebe als Ungrund"@de ;
    skos:definition "Love found is a supernatural, supersensual groundless abyss (Ungrund) with no place to dwell; incomparable, deeper than anything (Ichts), a nothing to all things because not graspable, therefore free from all things and the one good whose nature cannot be said."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: Ungrund; Ichts."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
