pmc:ChristianTheosophyLiebeWohntWoMenschWohnt a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Love dwells where man does not dwell"@en, "Liebe wohnt, wo der Mensch nicht wohnt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Where love dwells in man: where man does not dwell in himself, i.e. in the soul left to the ground (zu Grund gelassene Seele) that dies to its own will and wills nothing but what God wills; as far as the own will is dead, love takes the place it occupied; where nothing is, God's love alone works."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: zu Grund gelassene Seele."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 174, §28-29; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyGoettlicheLiebeLebenEigenenNatur a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Divine love as the life of one's nature"@en, "Göttliche Liebe als Leben der eigenen Natur"@de ;
    skos:definition "Divine love becoming the life of one's nature: one lives no longer by one's own will but by love's will; dead to oneself and living to God."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 174, §30; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmp:ChristianTheosophyLiebeGanzErgeben a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Wholly surrendering to love"@en, "Sich der Liebe ganz ergeben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Give oneself wholly and utterly to love instead of trying to grasp it; die to one's own will."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 174, §30; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyErgebungMachtLiebeLebenNatur a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Surrender makes love the life of one's nature"@en, "Ergebung macht die Liebe zum Leben der Natur"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wholly surrendering to love yields love becoming the life of one's nature."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChristianTheosophyLiebeGanzErgeben ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChristianTheosophyGoettlicheLiebeLebenEigenenNatur ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 174, §30; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyLiebeSetztSterbenEigenwillensVoraus a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Love requires death of the own will"@en, "Liebe setzt das Sterben des Eigenwillens voraus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Love cannot be obtained without the dying of one's own will; the disciple asks if it can, and the answer is that grasping drives it away, only surrender (death to own will) receives it."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChristianTheosophyLiebeGanzErgeben ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChristianTheosophyGoettlicheLiebeLebenEigenenNatur ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "If one wants to grasp it, it flees from one." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 174, §29-30; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyGreifenNachLiebeVertreibtSie a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Grasping at love drives it away"@en, "Greifen nach der Liebe vertreibt sie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wanting to grasp love makes it flee."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure; it concerns pmc:ChristianTheosophyGoettlicheLiebeLebenEigenenNatur."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: fassen."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 174, §30; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyLiebeEtwasSuchenWarumWenige a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeking love in Something; why few find it"@en, "Liebe im Etwas suchen; warum wenige sie finden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Why so few find love though all want it: they seek it in Something, in image-bound opinion, in own desire and natural lust; though it offers itself it finds no place in them because the image of the own will has taken its place; it dwells only in the Nothing."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure; it concerns pmc:ChristianTheosophyGoettlicheLiebeLebenEigenenNatur."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: bildliche Meynung; Bildlichkeit eigenes Willens."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 174, §31; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyAmtLiebeEtwasVerbrennen a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Office of love: burning the Something"@en, "Amt der Liebe: das Etwas verbrennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Office of love: it presses without ceasing into the Something, and where it finds a place that stands still it takes it, kindles a fire in the Something, burns it and over-inflames itself in it."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition implied: a place in the person that stands still."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: uber-inflammiren."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 175, §32; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyZeichenLiebeVerbrenntIchheit a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sign: love burning one's I-ness"@en, "Zeichen: Liebe verbrennt die Ichheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign: one will feel love burn one's I-ness and rejoice in one's fire so much that one would rather be killed than go back into one's Something; its flame would not leave one even at the cost of temporal life and would break hell for one's sake."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success, announced in advance."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: Ichheit."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 175, §33; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmp:ChristianTheosophyWeltZuwiderWandeln a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Walking contrary to the world"@en, "Der Welt zuwider wandeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Nearest way to love: go where the path is hardest; take up what the world discards; avoid what the world does; walk against the world in everything."@en ;
    skos:note "Word lost in OCR (\"in —— Dingen\"); sense \"in all things\" supplied by context and §35."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 175, §34; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyGegenwegNaechsterWegLiebe a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Contrary walking: nearest way to love"@en, "Gegenweg als nächster Weg zur Liebe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Walking contrary to the world is the nearest way to divine love becoming one's life."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChristianTheosophyWeltZuwiderWandeln ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChristianTheosophyGoettlicheLiebeLebenEigenenNatur ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 175, §34; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyGegenwegHeisstJemandemSchaden a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Contrary way does not mean harming anyone"@en, "Gegenweg heißt nicht, jemandem zu schaden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Limit on the contrary way: it does not mean harming anyone; it means walking alone on the right way, which is contrary to all the world's false ways."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChristianTheosophyWeltZuwiderWandeln ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 175, §35; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyKostenGegenwegsAngstAnscheinTorheit a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Cost of contrary way: anguish and seeming folly"@en, "Kosten des Gegenwegs: Angst und Anschein der Torheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Expected cost: the contrary way brings anguish and unrest according to the flesh and being taken for a fool by the world; the anguish gives occasion to continual repentance, and in such anguish love most gladly fans its fire."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChristianTheosophyWeltZuwiderWandeln ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 175, §35; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyInflammendeLiebesfeuerGottes a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The inflaming fire of God's love"@en, "Das inflammende Liebesfeuer Gottes"@de ;
    skos:definition "Attaining the inflaming fire of God's love: whiter than the sun, sweeter than anything, more strengthening than food and drink, lovelier than all joy of this world; whoever gains it surpasses any king in riches, nobler than any emperor and stronger than all power."@en ;
    skos:note "Continues to p. 176; one word garbled (\"ot oj als kein Kayser\")."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: inflammende Liebe."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 176, §35; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyGegenwegEntzuendetLiebesfeuer a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Contrary walking kindles love's fire"@en, "Gegenweg entzündet das Liebesfeuer"@de ;
    skos:definition "Walking the contrary way kindles the fire of love that the world mistakes for folly."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChristianTheosophyWeltZuwiderWandeln ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChristianTheosophyInflammendeLiebesfeuerGottes ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 176, §35; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyHimmelHoelleEinwendungWillens a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Heaven and hell as turning of the will"@en, "Himmel und Hölle als Einwendung des Willens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Heaven and hell are everywhere present and already within the soul; there is no travel into them at death, only a turning-in of the will into God's love or wrath, and this happens during the life of the body."@en ;
    skos:note "Owed because it states the condition (in this life) under which the decisive turning occurs."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: Einwendung des Willens."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 176, §36-37; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmp:ChristianTheosophyWillenGrundGottErgeben a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Yielding the will to the ground of God"@en, "Den Willen zu Grund Gott ergeben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Let the will yield itself to the ground of God so that it sinks out of itself, past every ground and place, and becomes a nothing to itself according to its own will."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: gelassener Wille."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 177, §38; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyGoettlicheRuheGelassenenWillen a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Divine rest in the resigned will"@en, "Göttliche Ruhe im gelassenen Willen"@de ;
    skos:definition "God working and willing in the resigned will and dwelling in it, the soul sanctified and come into divine rest."@en ;
    skos:note "After bodily death the soul is then penetrated with divine love and light like fire through iron (eschatological consequence, not separately recorded)."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: göttliche Ruhe."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 177, §38; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyErgebungGrundFuehrtGoettlicherRuhe a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Yielding to the ground yields divine rest"@en, "Ergebung zu Grund führt zu göttlicher Ruhe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Yielding the will to the ground of God yields divine rest with God dwelling in the resigned will."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChristianTheosophyWillenGrundGottErgeben ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChristianTheosophyGoettlicheRuheGelassenenWillen ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 177, §38; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyVerweigerteGelassenheitVerhindertGoettlicheRuhe a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Refusing resignation bars divine rest"@en, "Verweigerte Gelassenheit verhindert göttliche Ruhe"@de ;
    skos:definition "The godless soul that will not enter divine resignation (Gelassenheit) of its will but goes always into own lust, vanity and falsehood takes in malice, lies, pride, avarice, envy and wrath; this becomes manifest in it like fire in iron and it cannot come to divine rest, because God's wrath is manifest in it."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure; it concerns pmc:ChristianTheosophyGoettlicheRuheGelassenenWillen."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: Gelassenheit."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 177, §38; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyEwigesReuenUngelassenenSeeleNach a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Eternal regret for the unresigned soul after death"@en, "Ewiges Reuen der ungelassenen Seele nach dem Tod"@de ;
    skos:definition "Warning: for the soul that refused resignation, eternal regret and despair begin when the body separates; it is shut in its own wrath by its false desire, cannot see God's light and carries hell within itself wherever it goes."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChristianTheosophyWillenGrundGottErgeben ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 177, §38; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyAuchHeiligeEmpfindenFreudeHier a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Even saints feel joy only imperfectly in this life"@en, "Auch Heilige empfinden Freude hier nur unvollkommen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Expectation management: even the holy soul cannot perfectly feel the light and great joy in this life; it feels God's love in faith, but natural life wrapped in flesh and blood is sifted by world, devil and the curse of wrath, so the soul is often in anguish; it sinks into hope of grace and stands like a rose among thorns until death removes the hindrance."@en ;
    skos:note "Implies that recurring anguish is not by itself a sign of failure. Running head misprinted/misread as 17s."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChristianTheosophyGoettlicheRuheGelassenenWillen ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 178, §39; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyGottlosesGewissenFuehltHoelleOhne a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Godless conscience feels hell without understanding"@en, "Gottloses Gewissen fühlt die Hölle ohne Verständnis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Warning: the godless does feel hell in his false conscience but does not understand it, because earthly vanity and the light of outer nature still cover the pain; after death the soul stands in eternal hunger and thirst for the vanity it loved."@en ;
    skos:note "Continues to p. 179. Running head misprinted/misread as 17s."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChristianTheosophyWillenGrundGottErgeben ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 178, §39; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyEngelWohnenWoKeineSelbheit a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Angels dwelling where selfhood is absent"@en, "Engel wohnen, wo keine Selbheit ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Angels: they dwell with a person wherever he does not dwell according to selfhood and own will; they dwell in the revelation of God where God's will wills in a thing."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: Selbheit."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Engel" ;
    pm:nameRole "spiritual beings present wherever God's will is manifest in a thing; companions of the self-emptied person" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 179, §40-41; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyTeufelWohnenSelbheitEigenwillen a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Devils dwelling in selfhood and own will"@en, "Teufel wohnen in Selbheit und Eigenwillen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Devils: they dwell with a person wherever he dwells in selfhood and own will; where a thing has own will without God's will, there the devil dwells and all that is outside God."@en ;
    skos:note "Last word of the sentence clipped in OCR (\"übera\")."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Teuffel" ;
    pm:nameRole "beings dwelling in own will apart from God's will" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 179, §40-41; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyAeussereWeltDeckeGeistlichenWelt a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Outer world as cover over the spiritual world"@en, "Äußere Welt als Decke der geistlichen Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Why the spiritual world is not seen: man according to temporal life is only from the visible world, which is a cover over the spiritual world as the body covers the soul; therefore in outer life he does not see the spiritual world, which becomes manifest to the soul when the outer man dies."@en ;
    skos:note "Explains a limit of perception relevant to the capacities above."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: Decke."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
