pmc:ChristianTheosophyHimmelHoelleIneinanderTagNacht a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Heaven and hell interpenetrating like day and night"@en, "Himmel und Hölle ineinander wie Tag und Nacht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Heaven and hell interpenetrate like day and night, each a nothing to the other; heaven is the manifestation of the eternal One working in stillness, hell works in selfhood and false will."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 179, §42; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyEngelSeeleOffenbarungGoettlichenWillens a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Angel and soul as manifestation of divine will"@en, "Engel und Seele als Offenbarung göttlichen Willens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Angel and human soul: of the same origin, a piece of divine knowledge of the divine will, arising from the divine Word and led into a counter-image of divine love; darkness arises in the self-acceptance of own desire, light in willing together with God; they are simply the divine will made manifest, in light or darkness."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: Annehmlichkeit; Gegenwurff."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Engel; Seele eines Menschen" ;
    pm:nameRole "manifestation of the divine will, in light or darkness" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 180, §43; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyLeibBildSichtbarenWelt a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Body as image of the visible world"@en, "Leib als Bild der sichtbaren Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The human body equals the visible world and pictures the whole world; the visible world reveals the inner spiritual world of eternal light and darkness; God formed the outer man from the outer world and breathed the inner spiritual world into him as soul, so the soul can take up and work evil and good."@en ;
    skos:note "Continues to p. 181."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 180, §44; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyGleichheitsprinzipJedesWerkKehrtArt a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Principle of likeness: each work returns to its kind"@en, "Gleichheitsprinzip: jedes Werk kehrt in seine Art zurück"@de ;
    skos:definition "Principle of likeness: whatever is born of each will presses back into its likeness; works wrought by the spirit in this time separate at the end into light or darkness."@en ;
    skos:note "Recorded because it states the law linking present practice of the will to outcome."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 181, §45; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyGestufteAuferstehungsherrlichkeitSonneMondSterne a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Graded resurrection glory like sun, moon, stars"@en, "Gestufte Auferstehungsherrlichkeit wie Sonne, Mond, Sterne"@de ;
    skos:definition "Graded ranking of resurrection glory: all enjoy divine working, but power and illumination are very unequal, like sun, moon, stars and meadow flowers."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Jacob Böhme, in Vom übersinnlichen Leben" ;
    dcterms:date "1624"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 183, §49; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyAengstlichesWirkenGebaerungGoettlicherKraft a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Anxious working as birth of divine power"@en, "Ängstliches Wirken als Gebärung göttlicher Kraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "The creature's anxious working in the present time is an opening and birth of divine power, by which God's power becomes mobile and active; the degree of power and illumination after resurrection follows how far one was endowed with power in this anxious working."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: ängstliches Würcken."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 183, §49; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyVertrauenZugerechneteGenugtuungMindertVerherrlichung a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Relying on imputed satisfaction lessens glory"@en, "Vertrauen auf zugerechnete Genugtuung mindert die Verherrlichung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Condition of lesser outcome: those who only waited for an imputed satisfaction while serving the belly-god, and turned only at the end, will not have so great power and illumination as those who worked with Christ and not in fleshly lust."@en ;
    skos:note "Polemical against reliance on imputed satisfaction (forensic justification) but no author or group is named; not recorded as dispute."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure; it concerns pmc:ChristianTheosophyGestufteAuferstehungsherrlichkeitSonneMondSterne."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: zugerechnete Genugthuung."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 183, §49; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyChristusWohntGlaubenErgebenen a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Christ indwelling the faith of the yielded"@en, "Christus wohnt im Glauben der Ergebenen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Christ: dwells essentially in the faith of the wholly yielded, gives them his flesh as food and his blood as drink and possesses the ground of their faith inwardly; hence what is done to such a Christian in bodily need is done to Christ."@en ;
    skos:note "Continues to p. 186. Running head misprinted/misread as 181."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Christus" ;
    pm:nameRole "indwelling presence in the wholly yielded" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 185, §54; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyBeduerftigenAbweisenHeisstChristusAbweisen a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Refusing the needy is refusing Christ"@en, "Den Bedürftigen abweisen heißt Christus abweisen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Warning: whoever withdraws his hand from a needy Christian, refuses the poor, mocks or pushes him away, does this to Christ himself and despises him in his members."@en ;
    skos:note "Running head misprinted/misread as 181."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChristianTheosophyChristusWohntGlaubenErgebenen ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 185, §54; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyBedrueckerArmenErwartetHoellischeFeuer a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Oppressors of the poor face hell-fire"@en, "Bedrücker der Armen erwartet das höllische Feuer"@de ;
    skos:definition "Warning: those who torment the poor and consume their sweat in luxury persecute Christ in his members, enlarge the devil's kingdom and drive the poor into frivolous ways; unless they turn wholeheartedly to Christ and serve him they must go into hell-fire."@en ;
    skos:note "Running head of p. 186 lost in OCR; page placed by sequence."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChristianTheosophyChristusWohntGlaubenErgebenen ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 186, §55; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyGegenStreiterChristiReichMeinungen a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against quarrellers over Christ's kingdom and opinions"@en, "Gegen Streiter um Christi Reich und Meinungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Against those who in this time quarrel over the kingdom of Christ and persecute, shame and slander one another: they have never known Christ; every quarrel over opinions mirrors self-ownership; their useless wrangling seeks not love but image-bound self to be seen in opinions and moves princes to wars that devastate lands."@en ;
    skos:note "Group identified by conduct, not by party or author name; recorded as dispute because the opposition is explicit; flag as borderline. Continues to p. 187. Running head of p. 186 lost in OCR; page placed by sequence."@en ;
    skos:note "Entered as conceptualizing: only Böhme's side is read, and the party is described by its conduct, not named."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: Meynungen; bildliche Eigenheit."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 186, §56; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyOhneGlaubenDemutZornGewappnet a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Lacking faith and humility: armed only with wrath"@en, "Ohne Glauben und Demut: nur mit Zorn gewappnet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whoever lacks faith and humility and does not stand in Christ's spirit is armed only with God's wrath and serves the victory of image-bound selfhood; all zeal in strife that seeks self-interest rather than promoting love is of the devil."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: bildliche Eigenheit."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 187, §56; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophyWarumGottStreitZulaesstOffenbarung a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Why God permits strife: manifestation and free will"@en, "Warum Gott Streit zulässt: Offenbarung und freier Wille"@de ;
    skos:definition "Why God permits strife: life stands in strife so that it becomes manifest, perceptible and wisdom distinguishable and known; God leaves all in free will so that each life causes and awakens its own judgment in itself; the saints' joy has to come out of death as light from a candle through consumption in fire."@en ;
    skos:note "Continues to p. 188."@en ;
    skos:note "Term as printed: Empfindlichkeit und Schiedlichkeit."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 187, §57; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChristianTheosophySanftmutGruentSterbenEigenwillens a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Meekness greening through death of own will"@en, "Sanftmut grünt durch das Sterben des Eigenwillens"@de ;
    skos:definition "The holy life of meekness greens out through death, where the own will dies and God's love-will alone rules and acts in all."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChristianTheosophy ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:VomUebersinnlichenLeben ;
    dcterms:source "Böhme, Vom übersinnlichen Leben, the sixth booklet of Der Weg zu Christo, verfasset in neun Büchlein (no place, printed after the Amsterdam copy, 1732), p. 188, §57; read in a full-text layer of the open scan archive item derwegzuchristov00bohm whose running heads carry the page" .
